WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.199 --> 00:00:04.300
The Punisher has been a mainstay of Marvel
movies and television for decades.

00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:08.639
But there's one project fans never got to
see: Kurt Sutter's take on The Punisher 2,

00:00:08.639 --> 00:00:12.520
which was scrapped in favor of Punisher: War
Zone, which hit theaters in 2008.

00:00:12.520 --> 00:00:16.090
Sutter, of course, has since become famous
as the creator and executive producer of Sons

00:00:16.090 --> 00:00:19.910
of Anarchy, so we asked him for an exclusive
look back at what he had planned.

00:00:19.910 --> 00:00:23.360
Here's Kurt Sutter on the Punisher movie we
never got to see...

00:00:23.360 --> 00:00:25.070
Not Marvel Enough For Marvel

00:00:25.070 --> 00:00:27.920
Sutter was hired to do a simple polish of
the Punisher 2 screenplay.

00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:30.730
But he had his own ideas how the story should
go.

00:00:30.730 --> 00:00:33.820
He decided he was "gonna mix it up [and] make
it different."

00:00:33.820 --> 00:00:36.970
Marvel honcho Kevin Feige didn't appreciate
his tinkering with their characters.

00:00:36.970 --> 00:00:37.970
As Sutter told us:

00:00:37.970 --> 00:00:40.910
"They're two-dimensional for a reason: that's
the purpose they serve.

00:00:40.910 --> 00:00:44.730
So I was trying to expand the Marvel Universe
in a direction it should not have been expanded

00:00:44.730 --> 00:00:45.730
in."

00:00:45.730 --> 00:00:46.840
Less Guns, More Introspection

00:00:46.840 --> 00:00:48.870
So why did Sutter's vision fail?

00:00:48.870 --> 00:00:52.530
He explained it was because he wanted it to
be more about character, and less about formulaic

00:00:52.530 --> 00:00:53.530
action, saying:

00:00:53.530 --> 00:00:57.290
"I was trying to write to the emotionality
of this dude and motivate the absurd violence

00:00:57.290 --> 00:00:58.840
with some kind of meaning."

00:00:58.840 --> 00:01:02.760
His efforts included writing in a love interest
in order to, as he put it, "explore that pain

00:01:02.760 --> 00:01:03.800
through that relationship."

00:01:03.800 --> 00:01:07.009
"Who punishes you?"

00:01:07.009 --> 00:01:11.969
But Sutter's efforts were at cross purposes
with Marvel's vision for the film.

00:01:11.969 --> 00:01:13.109
Sutter said,

00:01:13.109 --> 00:01:16.990
"There's only X amount of time the movies,
so you have moments of that, but you can't

00:01:16.990 --> 00:01:19.350
really have a subplot that explores that kind
of thing.

00:01:19.350 --> 00:01:21.810
Not in a summer blockbuster or a Marvel picture."

00:01:32.770 --> 00:01:34.619
Kevin Feige Was Not Amused

00:01:34.619 --> 00:01:38.560
After Sutter turned in his radically different
script, he had the uncomfortable experience

00:01:38.560 --> 00:01:41.999
of going over it with producer Gale Anne Hurd
and Kevin Feige.

00:01:41.999 --> 00:01:42.999
Sutter told us:

00:01:42.999 --> 00:01:46.779
"I think they realized what I was trying to
do…and how wrong that was.

00:01:46.779 --> 00:01:50.509
So they tried to guide me back, and like I
said, I did another pass, but poor Gale Anne

00:01:50.509 --> 00:01:51.509
Hurd…

00:01:51.509 --> 00:01:54.420
We were sitting at a big table, and I think
she started glancing over at Kevin, going

00:01:54.420 --> 00:01:55.899
'I don't know what happened!'"

00:01:55.899 --> 00:01:57.829
Shortly after, Sutter was fired.

00:01:57.829 --> 00:02:03.259
"And at the end of it, The Punisher will be
dead!"

00:02:03.259 --> 00:02:04.469
Better On TV

00:02:04.469 --> 00:02:07.790
The only piece of Sutter's script to make
it into the final version of Punisher: War

00:02:07.790 --> 00:02:10.679
Zone was the origin of the bad guy, Jigsaw.

00:02:10.679 --> 00:02:14.850
The film was a failure, but the character's
return in 2016 on the second season of Daredevil

00:02:14.850 --> 00:02:18.750
was popular enough to earn Punisher his own
Netflix series starring Jon Bernthal.

00:02:18.750 --> 00:02:21.989
So why was Punisher more successful on television
than film?

00:02:21.989 --> 00:02:25.650
Sutter thinks the character is just better
suited to the small screen, telling us that,

00:02:25.650 --> 00:02:30.390
"as powerful a character as Frank Castle is,
there's a real linear component to that narrative,

00:02:30.390 --> 00:02:34.299
and it almost works better tangentially, alongside
of another story, rather than standing up

00:02:34.299 --> 00:02:35.299
on its own…

00:02:35.299 --> 00:02:37.799
That's what you're able to do with TV: you
can go sideways.

00:02:37.799 --> 00:02:39.269
You just can't go sideways in a feature.

00:02:39.269 --> 00:02:40.700
Not unless it's an indie.

00:02:40.700 --> 00:02:43.970
But in terms of Hollywood, the narrative has
to be moving forward."

00:02:43.970 --> 00:02:44.970
Thanks for watching!

00:02:44.970 --> 00:02:47.890
Subscribe to our YouTube channel to watch
more videos like the one you just saw.

00:02:47.890 --> 00:02:50.680
And leave us a comment to let us know which
version of Punisher is your favorite…

